{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BVDWa6aJHRn2ubNGF9FAKb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu workout_doc hr target \"%lthr\" range \"start\" \"end\" \"value\" JSON format API\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157\"},{\"title\":\"HR target missing from Garmin Connect workout upload\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-missing-from-garmin-connect-workout-upload/5483\"},{\"title\":\"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/need-help-with-hr-based-workouts-in-bpm/120685\"},{\"title\":\"Setting Lactate Threshold HR/Power\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/setting-lactate-threshold-hr-power/5803\"}]\n\nThe search turned up forum posts, not official API documentation, so the exact `%lthr` HR step format isn't confirmed.\n\n- **Power example:** A forum user shows a `workout_doc` with an `ftp` field, `\"target\": \"POWER\"`, and steps using a `power` object with `value` and `units`, plus a `_power` object with `start` and `end` values. For power the athlete's FTP is included in the workout_doc field. I didn't find an HR example with `%lthr` units.\n- **Ranges:** Intervals.icu converts fixed targets into ranges. The default range for power and pace is 2.5%. For HR it is 1.5%. You can override this with the `hrRange` query parameter, and use 0.0 to disable range.\n- **LTHR field:** A developer said they have added these fields to workout_doc, including an `lthr` integer and a `threshold_pace` float. I didn't find a dated changelog confirming this.\n- **Undocumented JSON posting:** One user said even though its not documented posting with JSON works. Another forum reply recommends Posting Intervals.icu text is the best way if you can because all features are supported.\n- **Garmin mismatch:** A Garmin-related thread reports that the target HR is sent as % of LTHR and if the sending or receiving app have different LTHR, it doesn't work as intended.\n\nFor authoritative field names, check the Intervals.icu API docs or the forum thread \"API access to Intervals.icu\" (topic 609) directly, or inspect a downloaded workout's JSON in the web app.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1f702b3-7077-4fb5-9fbb-50f260787b45","uuid":"8cfe1ff6-f02e-438a-9ea9-65302fd948bd","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:20:37.539Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu workout_doc hr target \"%lthr\" range \"start\" \"end\" \"value\" JSON format API","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015nsGVRnCoEggHWhkMVMZUU","content":[{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389"},{"title":"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356"},{"title":"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157"},{"title":"HR target missing from Garmin Connect workout upload","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/hr-target-missing-from-garmin-connect-workout-upload/5483"},{"title":"Need help with HR-based workouts (in bpm)","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/need-help-with-hr-based-workouts-in-bpm/120685"},{"title":"Setting Lactate Threshold HR/Power","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/setting-lactate-threshold-hr-power/5803"}]},"The search turned up forum posts, not official API documentation, so the exact `%lthr` HR step format isn't confirmed.\n\n- **Power example:** A forum user shows a `workout_doc` with an `ftp` field, `\"target\": \"POWER\"`, and steps using a `power` object with `value` and `units`, plus a `_power` object with `start` and `end` values. For power the athlete's FTP is included in the workout_doc field. I didn't find an HR example with `%lthr` units.\n- **Ranges:** Intervals.icu converts fixed targets into ranges. The default range for power and pace is 2.5%. For HR it is 1.5%. You can override this with the `hrRange` query parameter, and use 0.0 to disable range.\n- **LTHR field:** A developer said they have added these fields to workout_doc, including an `lthr` integer and a `threshold_pace` float. I didn't find a dated changelog confirming this.\n- **Undocumented JSON posting:** One user said even though its not documented posting with JSON works. Another forum reply recommends Posting Intervals.icu text is the best way if you can because all features are supported.\n- **Garmin mismatch:** A Garmin-related thread reports that the target HR is sent as % of LTHR and if the sending or receiving app have different LTHR, it doesn't work as intended.\n\nFor authoritative field names, check the Intervals.icu API docs or the forum thread \"API access to Intervals.icu\" (topic 609) directly, or inspect a downloaded workout's JSON in the web app."],"durationSeconds":7.531490000000002,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BVDWa6aJHRn2ubNGF9FAKb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
