{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JteMpq7hZvQRf9MBsdwEuA","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-cCsa6P/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1f702b3-7077-4fb5-9fbb-50f260787b45","uuid":"e2fc5235-beb6-474d-a4a7-f1fcb4cd4ed2","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:20:50.423Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-cCsa6P/README.md","oldString":"Athlete thresholds live in Intervals (LTHR 172 for this athlete). HR targets\nin plans are percentages of LTHR; Intervals converts them to bpm at export.","newString":"Athlete thresholds: LTHR 172 for this athlete. Plans express HR targets as\npercentages of LTHR, and `gen.py` converts them to absolute bpm (`LTHR` constant\nin `gen.py`) before posting, so the watch does not re-resolve them against its\nown auto-detected LTHR/zones.","originalFile":"# tri-planner\n\nGenerates structured triathlon workouts and pushes them to Intervals.icu, which\nexports them to the athlete's Garmin watch through Garmin Connect.\n\n- `gen.py` turns a plan (`plans/*.json`) into the body for\n  `POST /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events` (an event with `workout_doc`).\n- `push.sh` posts it (needs `INTERVALS_API_KEY` and `ATHLETE_ID`).\n- `readback/` holds what the API returned for the last pushed event and\n  notes on what the watch displayed.\n\nAthlete thresholds live in Intervals (LTHR 172 for this athlete). HR targets\nin plans are percentages of LTHR; Intervals converts them to bpm at export.\n\n```\npython3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json\n./push.sh event.json\n```\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":9,"oldLines":8,"newStart":9,"newLines":10,"lines":[" - `readback/` holds what the API returned for the last pushed event and","   notes on what the watch displayed."," ","-Athlete thresholds live in Intervals (LTHR 172 for this athlete). HR targets","-in plans are percentages of LTHR; Intervals converts them to bpm at export.","+Athlete thresholds: LTHR 172 for this athlete. Plans express HR targets as","+percentages of LTHR, and `gen.py` converts them to absolute bpm (`LTHR` constant","+in `gen.py`) before posting, so the watch does not re-resolve them against its","+own auto-detected LTHR/zones."," "," ```"," python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JteMpq7hZvQRf9MBsdwEuA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS2E2ViDvffygdyhEaTk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GeY68EAqreNRvUofBocyVP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-cCsa6P/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR ranges clamped to watch zones — fix\n\n## Cause\n\n`gen.py` emitted each HR target as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`\nand left the conversion to Intervals/Garmin. The watch auto-detects its own\nLTHR (168 here, not 172), and the %LTHR targets reach it as its own zone\nbands, so every corridor came back as a zone edge (118–137, 137–151, 151–162)\ninstead of the planned bpm range.\n\n## Change (`gen.py`)\n\n- Added an `LTHR = 172` constant and a `pct_to_bpm()` helper that rounds\n  `pct * LTHR / 100` to the nearest bpm using integer math.\n- `hr_target()` now emits `{\"units\": \"bpm\", \"value\": <lo bpm>, \"end\": <hi bpm>}`.\n- Kept the `value`/`end` keys and the rest of the document structure unchanged,\n  since the API already accepted that shape (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`).\n\n## Result for `plans/tempo-run.json`\n\nChecked by running `gen.py` and reading the targets back:\n\n| step | planned (% LTHR) | emitted (bpm) | expected on watch (from notes) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Warm-up easy | 68–75 | 117–129 | 117–129 |\n| Tempo | 88–93 | 151–160 | 151–160 |\n| Float | 75–82 | 129–141 | 129–141 |\n| Cool-down | 65–72 | 112–124 | 112–124 |\n\nRounding: 0.68×172 = 116.96 → 117, 0.93×172 = 159.96 → 160, and so on.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- I have not pushed the event or checked it on the watch. The ground rules\n  rule out reporting to external services, and I have no API key here. The fix\n  is based on the readback notes plus the arithmetic above, not on a live\n  re-test.\n- The notes say an earlier `units: \"bpm\"` attempt showed 214–249 bpm. I can't\n  reproduce that from the repo, and nothing here explains it. If the new payload\n  still shows wrong numbers, compare it with that earlier payload first.\n- If the watch later changes LTHR, the bpm values will not follow it. That is\n  the trade-off for pinning the corridors; update `LTHR` in `gen.py` if the\n  athlete's LTHR in Intervals changes.\n\n## Files\n\n- `gen.py` — LTHR constant, `pct_to_bpm()`, `hr_target()` now emits bpm.\n- `README.md` — the line claiming Intervals converts %LTHR at export is replaced\n  with the new behaviour.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2256,"cache_read_input_tokens":27071,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2256},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1f702b3-7077-4fb5-9fbb-50f260787b45","uuid":"07b6290c-f02e-42f2-9f97-3c2063f1f6ef","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:20:54.321Z","request_id":"req_011CgS2E269pEUJTMZh8iTqj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GeY68EAqreNRvUofBocyVP":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-cCsa6P/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR ranges clamped to watch zones — fix\n\n## Cause\n\n`gen.py` emitted each HR target as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`\nand left the conversion to Intervals/Garmin. The watch auto-detects its own\nLTHR (168 here, not 172), and the %LTHR targets reach it as its own zone\nbands, so every corridor came back as a zone edge (118–137, 137–151, 151–162)\ninstead of the planned bpm range.\n\n## Change (`gen.py`)\n\n- Added an `LTHR = 172` constant and a `pct_to_bpm()` helper that rounds\n  `pct * LTHR / 100` to the nearest bpm using integer math.\n- `hr_target()` now emits `{\"units\": \"bpm\", \"value\": <lo bpm>, \"end\": <hi bpm>}`.\n- Kept the `value`/`end` keys and the rest of the document structure unchanged,\n  since the API already accepted that shape (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`).\n\n## Result for `plans/tempo-run.json`\n\nChecked by running `gen.py` and reading the targets back:\n\n| step | planned (% LTHR) | emitted (bpm) | expected on watch (from notes) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Warm-up easy | 68–75 | 117–129 | 117–129 |\n| Tempo | 88–93 | 151–160 | 151–160 |\n| Float | 75–82 | 129–141 | 129–141 |\n| Cool-down | 65–72 | 112–124 | 112–124 |\n\nRounding: 0.68×172 = 116.96 → 117, 0.93×172 = 159.96 → 160, and so on.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- I have not pushed the event or checked it on the watch. The ground rules\n  rule out reporting to external services, and I have no API key here. The fix\n  is based on the readback notes plus the arithmetic above, not on a live\n  re-test.\n- The notes say an earlier `units: \"bpm\"` attempt showed 214–249 bpm. I can't\n  reproduce that from the repo, and nothing here explains it. If the new payload\n  still shows wrong numbers, compare it with that earlier payload first.\n- If the watch later changes LTHR, the bpm values will not follow it. That is\n  the trade-off for pinning the corridors; update `LTHR` in `gen.py` if the\n  athlete's LTHR in Intervals changes.\n\n## Files\n\n- `gen.py` — LTHR constant, `pct_to_bpm()`, `hr_target()` now emits bpm.\n- `README.md` — the line claiming Intervals converts %LTHR at export is replaced\n  with the new behaviour.\n"}}}
